Build the standalone library from LLVM's CMake package instead of llvm-config, which
cannot run when cross-compiling and reports the build machine's system libraries; make
its name configurable; support Windows (exports through a generated module definition
file, DLL installed in bin) and FreeBSD (no -z defs).

To be upstreamed into LLVM.jl's deps/LLVMExtra, after which this patch goes away.
